; ===============  linux
## rtfm man pages
; RTFM means "read the manual". Every Linux command and function has a man page.
; Read it first: it is the real answer, written by the people who made the tool.
man PAGE                           # read the manual page of a command or function  @rtfm @help @docs  <man:man(1)>
https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/  # read Linux man pages online (commands, syscalls, libc)  @rtfm @manpages @docs  <https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/>

## bash
; Bash is the shell: the program that reads and runs the commands you type.
; Read these to learn its rules and to write your own scripts.
https://www.gnu.org/software/bash/manual/html_node/index.html  # read the official GNU Bash manual  @shell @rtfm @docs  <https://www.gnu.org/software/bash/manual/html_node/index.html>
https://bash.cyberciti.biz/guide/Main_Page  # learn bash scripting step by step with examples  @shell @tutorial @guide  <https://bash.cyberciti.biz/guide/Main_Page>
